    whatIsIt: "A 3D alternating-current (AC) electronics bench that lets you tune driving frequency f, resistance R, inductance L, and capacitance C to observe reactance, phase shift \u03C6, impedance Z, and series resonance.",
    howDoesItWork: "In a series AC circuit driven by V(t) = V_peak sin(2\u03C0ft), a resistor opposes current in phase (X_R = R, \u0394\u03C6 = 0\xB0), an inductor opposes changes in current with inductive reactance X_L = 2\u03C0fL (V_L leads I by +90\xB0), and a capacitor stores oscillating charge with capacitive reactance X_C = 1/(2\u03C0fC) (V_C lags I by \u221290\xB0). Total circuit impedance is Z = \u221A(R\xB2 + (X_L \u2212 X_C)\xB2) and the phase angle between source voltage and current is \u03C6 = arctan((X_L \u2212 X_C)/R). At the ideal series-RLC resonance frequency f\u2080 = 1/(2\u03C0\u221A(LC)), X_L equals X_C so reactive voltages cancel, impedance reaches its minimum Z = R, phase difference vanishes (\u03C6 = 0\xB0), and RMS current I_rms = V_rms / Z peaks.",
